    nvidia-cuda-runtime                         -                12.9.79
    the resolved stack matches what this example was last verified against

    pinned 0.1.7, and that is still the newest release upstream

    Why a CUDA 12 stack runs here at all: the wheels ship their own CUDA runtime
    (nvidia-cuda-runtime-cu12 above), and the driver is backward compatible, so the
    container's CUDA toolkit is never used by the venv. The GPU driver is shared.
    The package index publishes only `cuda12` builds, up to `trt109` -- there is no
    cuda13 or TensorRT 11 artifact to install, so this is the only possible arrangement.
